Fix: split clauses robustly by finding markers in order at increasing positions: iterate letters, take the first occurrence after the previous marker. Only require the first occurrence of each letter in order. Let me rewrite split_clauses:

```
def split_clauses(defn):
    spans=[]
    pos=0
    for letter in 'abcdef':
        m=re.search(r'\(%s\)' % letter, defn[pos:])
        if not m: return None
        start=pos+m.start()
        spans.append((letter,start))
        pos=start+1
    out={}
    for i,(letter,start) in enumerate(spans):
        end=spans[i+1][1] if i+1<len(spans) else len(defn)
        out[letter]=defn[start:end].strip()
    return out
```
